{"id": "EUVD-2026-81781", "enisaUuid": "a549120b-6d38-3bab-a71c-b2455083bc46", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnull_blk: free global tag_set on init error path\n\nIf shared_tags is enabled, null_setup_tagset() allocates the global tag_set\nvia null_init_global_tag_set(). If device creation later fails, err_dev\ndestroys the default devices and calls unregister_blkdev(), but never frees\nthe global tag_set. Since module init failed, null_exit() is never invoked,\nso the global tag_set's tags and maps are permanently leaked.\n\nFree the global tag_set in err_dev, matching null_exit() which does\nif (tag_set.ops) blk_mq_free_tag_set(&tag_set).", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:59:24", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b2faa330184340d9418ad2c627c2ae881772e33", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/665c94554ff0d5d88caae7f40c16c8e0a3369eda", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2882e1450fa4597811a951196e07553ea134eb31", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b59484ac1e64dd78dbe8c6140891c6308085a75", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/081cf37e8a0e00cd91d6df53172c9d928790a798", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5a1c5ff3a49ba93a1fd0b70537e7a0164071760d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jmg2-qcvp-f7gg", "CVE-2026-90188"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04ae68e8-f562-3344-bf37-ec4fc05de221", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "11fd7789-07f3-34ae-8fbc-78a2008b7724", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82f402fefa50f1675bf918bcd009981bd6b30ac8 <0b2faa330184340d9418ad2c627c2ae881772e33"}, {"id": "33d2ee13-4f49-35fa-90b0-0d7d6b1a3738", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82f402fefa50f1675bf918bcd009981bd6b30ac8 <2882e1450fa4597811a951196e07553ea134eb31"}, {"id": "349184b8-619e-3c32-8d46-e76bdeb162b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "3e054e4f-0f9f-3ebc-9ee1-9d5fd859f7d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "49a9516d-a372-390f-bc3d-b0ace3db49ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "6d568601-37e3-33e2-90cd-45bd77af1a9c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "8d5fcd10-e30c-3904-be87-1830f2a4357c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82f402fefa50f1675bf918bcd009981bd6b30ac8 <081cf37e8a0e00cd91d6df53172c9d928790a798"}, {"id": "a2cc61da-e97b-3977-acc8-b4d8ccb19587", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "ce1d788f-1949-3cf1-a373-7dc566be5e44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "cfdad06d-a099-3713-9c3e-14de5e73e29b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82f402fefa50f1675bf918bcd009981bd6b30ac8 <665c94554ff0d5d88caae7f40c16c8e0a3369eda"}, {"id": "d0d1b7dc-ac24-37ef-a3c2-c4467c7959ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82f402fefa50f1675bf918bcd009981bd6b30ac8 <5a1c5ff3a49ba93a1fd0b70537e7a0164071760d"}, {"id": "f7d161bd-3760-3072-a81b-0e828c53793c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.13"}, {"id": "f94c263f-8c1d-3e2d-be08-849b068140a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "82f402fefa50f1675bf918bcd009981bd6b30ac8 <2b59484ac1e64dd78dbe8c6140891c6308085a75"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a6ace431-d2c1-3684-9750-ea6cc01f45f4", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}